337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic_61,337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic,182,337X393,null,"Part Condition: Fair Part Description: Gas Turbine T1 and T2 Bearings: • Both bearings were disassembled, visually inspected, penetrant tested, ultra-sonic tested, and replaced with refurbished bearing from PME. Both bearings were found with babbitt scoring marks. The slinger rings were in poor condition, especially on T2 (babbitt cracking and smearing). Bearing shop report is included in this document. PT and UT inspection reports are attached. • New TCs were installed and QC'd by site I&C upon close out. As requested by the customer, T2 thermocouples were routed through an instrumentation cable the customer installed with Bentley Nevada. The new route goes through the T2 cover plate and the bearing tunnel conduit. This work was completed by the on-site electricians, TRS. New packing glands were installed by customer I&C. • Opening and closing clearances were recorded. • With the exception of the air deflector (1S6), all of the oil seals/deflectors were replaced with a new set. The outgoing parts were found with excessive ID measurements, bent teeth, and showed evidence of oil leaking by. • Both journals measured to be nominal sized at 16.500"" • Lift hoses on both bearings were replaced. The closing lift readings were: • T1: 0.004"" • T2: 0.003"" Oil Seals 1S7 Oil Seals 1S7 Oil Seals 1S7 Oil Seals 1S7 Oil Seals 1S8 Oil Seals 1S8 Oil Seals 1S8 Oil Seals 1S9 Oil Seals 1S9 Oil Seals 1S9 Oil Seals 1S10 Oil Seals 1S10 Oil Seals 1S10 Oil Seals 1S10 As Found T1 LH As Found T1 LH As Found T1 LH As Found T1 LH As Found T1 UH As Found T2 LH As Found T2 LH As Found T2 LH As Found T2 LH As Found T2 UH T1 Lift Hose Installed T1 As Left T2 As Left T1 As Left T2 - Before UH Bearing Cap Install Bearings MS 7001F Closing Bearing & Seal Clearances, No. 1 Date 4/16/2022 Turbine S/N 298613 Prepared by Brian Schmalz FSR # 10363085 Sketches Enclosed? no Photos Enclosed? no Data Type opening • All axial clearances are measured with rotor against the loaded thrust face. Refer to EM5260 to confirm rotor position. • All views with turbine flow. SEAL INSPECTION Clearances Visual Inspection DIM Left Right Top Bottom Condition Disposition Comments 1S1 0.028 0.028 1S2 0.029 0.030 1S3 0.027 0.027 1S4 0.030 0.024 1S5 0.030 0.022 1S6 0.031 0.025 1S7* 0.009 1S8* 0.006 1S9* 0.008 1S10* 0.006 1WF1 0.027 0.028 DIM Description Measurement Insp. Date T1 Rotor Float 4/24/2022 * Measure total ring clearance at T1S Inactive Thrust U.H. .550"" 4/25/2022 each location. Shim Thickness L.H. .550"" 4/26/2022 TAS Active Thrust U.H. .464"" 4/27/2022 Shim Thickness L.H. .464"" 4/28/2022 Comments: .015"" Z INSPECTION REPORT CONDITION CODE M - Missing Metal W - Worn CR - Cracked DISPOSITION CODE N - No Repair or Replacement Necessary R - Repaired RN - Replaced with New Component Seal spec: 1S1, 1S2-.022""-.034"" 1S7, 1S8: .006''-.016'' 1S3: .016""-.032"" 1S9, 1S10: .005''-.013'' 1S4,1S5,1S6: .018""-.036"" 1WF1: .022""-.034"" GT71F103 T1S 1S1 1 WF1 T1 TAS #1 BRG. 1S2 1S7* LOADED THRUST FACE 1S8* 1S9* 1S3 1S4 1S5 1S6 1S10* CL Bearing & Seal Clearances No. 1 CLOSING GE Energy Services Company Proprietary Information Bearing & Seal Clearances No. 1 CL… Bearings MS 7001F Opening Bearing & Seal Clearances, No. 1 Date 4/16/2022 Turbine S/N 298613 Prepared by Brian Schmalz FSR # 10363085 Sketches Enclosed? no Photos Enclosed? no Data Type opening • All axial clearances are measured with rotor against the loaded thrust face. Refer to EM5260 to confirm rotor position. • All views with turbine flow. SEAL INSPECTION Clearances Visual Inspection DIM Left Right Top Bottom Condition Disposition Comments 1S1 0.024 0.027 1S2 0.024 0.029 1S3 0.024 0.024 1S4 0.024 0.021 1S5 0.023 0.021 1S6 0.025 0.018 1S7* 0.010 1S8* 1S9* 0.005 1S10* 0.003 1WF1 0.024 0.030 DIM Description Measurement Insp. Date T1 Rotor Float * Measure total ring clearance at T1S Inactive Thrust U.H. each location. Shim Thickness L.H. TAS Active Thrust U