337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic_67,337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic,227,337X393,null,"Part Condition: Good Part Description: The generator was disassembled for the planned MAGIC scope. The collector end was disassembled up to the main body fan blades (including removing both halves of the inner gas shield). The turbine end disassembly was identical except for the lower half inner gas shield. • Oil Deflectors • The outer, inner, and mid oil deflectors were all replaced (except for the CE outer oil deflector) due to heavy wear and signs of oil leaking by on the lower half. • The new deflectors were visually inspected and measured prior to disassembly. Alignment readings from oil deflector to journal were recorded at reassembly. • Hydrogen Seals and Casing • The H2 seals were found with pitting and scoring on the babbitt. All of the seals and springs were replaced with a new set. All seals were lapped to its respective H2 casing surface for 100% contact. • The H2 casing was cleaned and dimensions measured. The TE casing had a step and pitting on the sealing surface and sent to Gilberts Machine Shop to machine down the following surface to remove the defect: • Turbine End H2 Casing • Gas side surface: removed 0.003” • Air side surface: removed 0.003” • New anti rotation pins were installed on both casings. • The collector end H2 casing was meggered at reassembly, no issues. • CE and TE end shields were cleaned and reinstalled. Dow corning was pumped after it was bolted down. • The CE main body fan blades and bolting were removed, cleaned, and NDE'd. No indications were found. • All collector fan blades were found with tip rubs and rolled metal. A new set of collector fans and lock tabs were installed. • Both collector studs were found leaking and were replaced by the generator specialist and on-site winders. • Due to a leak, the field bore plug on the collector end was removed to replace the o- rings and reinstalled. • The TE GIB key expansion joint was found ripped and a new piece was installed. • Turbine end bearing cap found with bad lifting threads and a new 3/4"" - 10 helicoil was installed. While performing the generator air test, oil was seen inside the liquid leak detector due to misaligned seal oil valves. Two hydrogen coolers were removed to clean up the oil and reinstalled with new dow corning pumped in. Air test was redone using the reference chamber and passed the leak test. The generator was aligned as per TIL 1611-R2, Drawing 131T7734. As Found TE Gas Side As Found TE Gas Side As Found TE Gas Side As Found TE Air Side As Found TE Air Side As Found TE Air Side As Found CE Gas Side As Found CE Gas Side CE Gas Side Anti-Rotation Pin Slot Damage As Found CE Air Side As Found CE Air Side Collector Fan Tip Rubs Collector Fan Tip Rubs Collector Fan Tip Rubs New Collector Fans CE H2 Case Megger CE H2 Case Megger H2 Cooler Removed H2 Cooler Removed H2 Coolers Close Out Bore Plug O-Ring Replacement Bore Plug O-Ring Replacement As Found TE GIB Key Expansion Joint H2 Seals and Anti-Rotation Spring New Helicoil Installed - TE Bearing Cap Generator Field Clearance 7FH2 Collector End Date 4/29/2022 Generator Serial No. 337X393 Prepared by Project ID # 10363085 Turbine Serial No. 298613 Units recorded in 6 0.043 6 0.054 12 0.027 12 0.034 17 0.053 17 0.053 18 0.066 18 0.065 24 0.067 24 0.057 5 0.058 5 0.067 Comments: Willie Tang Inches Opening Clearances Closing Clearances D316321 FieldCore Proprietary Information Generator Fan Clearances Generator Field Clearance 7FH2 Turbine End Date 4/29/2022 Generator Serial No. 337X393 Prepared by Project ID # 10363085 Turbine Serial No",2026-04-13T02:36:43.024Z,2026-04-13T02:36:43.024Z,"[0.019923731684684753,-0.008835943415760994,-0.0068065025843679905,0.002275011967867613,-0.02681826800107956,0.009730193763971329,-0.029783660545945168,0.02463129162788391,0.005346973426640034,0.06201377138495445,0.028690172359347343,-0.01682860217988491,0.032489582896232605,0.032322779297828674,-0.019812528043985367,0.05