337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic_74,337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic,254,337X393,null,"Part Condition: Fair Part Description: Back Ground MAGIC utilizes a high intensity light source and two high resolution video cameras to view stator core laminations, stator windings, field surfaces, and wedges. A flexible borescope with digital high resolution is used to inspect coil end windings, the inboard ends of the retaining rings, and the stator high voltage leads and connections. A visual inspection of these components can provide data to assess the severity of rotor component heating related to unusual negative sequence operation; investigate high rotor vibration related to cooling flow inconsistencies; and evaluate stator core, stator bar, slot support problems, or surface contamination along with a wedge tightness assessment. Testing is performed to accurately quantify stator wedge tightness and is used to assess the need for wedge tightening or replacement. A “tight” stator winding can last two or three times as long as a winding that is not firmly held in the stator core. Test results are used to generate a “wedge tightness map,” which clearly shows the wedge tightness within the generator. The GT8 generator was found to be in overall fair condition with the wedge tightness report indicating a tight wedge system still remains in the generator, however there are several areas of concern where greasing can be seen on the wedge system. These areas should be cleaned and revisited when a rotor out inspection is scheduled in the future. There are areas throughout the generator which contain foreign material that was identified in a previous inspection report in 2015 which was identified as a white rag, pieces of this rag are still visible within the generator air duct regions of the stator core and also need to be revisited and removed on a future rotor out inspection to prevent the blocking of cooling gas in these regions. The end winding regions on both the collector end and turbine end are overall in good condition however there is heavy oil present on both ends of the generator which can cause greasing of several components on the end winding system in the future. The end windings should be cleaned of as much oil as possible on a future rotor out inspection. g GE Power Inspection & Life Extension Services Magic Photo I.D.Worksheet Job # 10363085 1 River Road, Bldg. 55 Rm",2026-04-13T02:36:43.024Z,2026-04-13T02:36:43.024Z,"[0.021077729761600494,-0.013826051726937294,-0.0009792700875550508,0.009256500750780106,-0.021637635305523872,0.026568416506052017,-0.02429267205297947,0.004264763556420803,0.013762837275862694,0.035201795399188995,0.04338363930583,-0.009798345156013966,0.027236690744757652,0.023227045312523842,-0.024581653997302055,0.0441422238945961,-0.02640586346387863,0.007784491870552301,-0.006985271815210581,-0.010078297927975655,-0.025538912042975426,0.010511772707104683,0.016381749883294106,0.03198685497045517,-0.017953097820281982,0.0020612648222595453,-0.010773664340376854,-0.0016672990750521421,0.037242744117975235,-0.027886902913451195,0.016137920320034027,0.036032624542713165,0.005946737714111805,0.027760472148656845,0.015668321400880814,-0.019831489771604538,-0.0023637942504137754,0.020373333245515823,0.023389598354697227,0.00372743490152061,-0.029873663559556007,-0.06415432691574097,-0.01199281308799982,0.03709825128316879,0.017275791615247726,-0.0079470444470644,-0.018729740753769875,-0.02118609845638275,-0.01357319112867117,0.01813371106982231,-0.017149360850453377,-0.003747754031792283,-0.024003688246011734,0.05458175018429756,0.04475631192326546,-0.0213125292211771,0.04063829779624939,0.1586519181728363,0.01490973960608244,-0.014972954988479614,0.009355839341878891,0.0009070242522284389,-0.028735792264342308,0.0003595360612962395,0.02721862867474556,0.0003727999283000827,-0.017022931948304176,-0.00931971613317728,-0.021764066070318222,0.02804945595562458,-0.02580983377993107,-0.026423923671245575,-0.007278770674020052,0.0