337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic_84,337X393 2022-04-04 Robotic,293,337X393,null,"Part Condition: Good Part Description: Body A visual inspection was performed on the field body utilizing the MAGIC Jr. The following items were inspected, but not limited to: • Vent slots for blockages/flow obstructions. • Field body wedges for signs of wear, movement, overheating or electrical discharge. • General cleanliness. • Balance plugs installed and proper staking. • Any other abnormalities The only discrepancy found was excessive oil contamination towards the turbine end of the core. Inspection of the field body should be done in accordance with GEK 103566. End Turns A visual inspection was performed under the collector end retaining rings. The following was inspected, but not limited to: • Flexible main lead for cracks, overheating, or signs of electrical discharge. • Main lead locking nut for dusting/signs of looseness. • Pole and coil jumpers for cracks, overheating, or signs of electrical discharge. • Distance blocking for proper alignment. • Turn insulation for signs of migration or damage. • General cleanliness. No discrepancies were noted. An inspection under the retaining rings should be performed in accordance with GEK 103566. Retaining Ring Retaining ring surfaces were inspected and were found to be in good condition. Nothing further to document or take action on. Collector Assembly The brushes were removed from the brush rigging assembly prior to electrical testing of the field. Upon inspection of the collector regions no signs of heavy carbon noted or improper wear on collector rings to be noted. Collector maintenance should be performed in accordance with GEK 116362. Field Winding Electrical testing was performed on the field, consisting of: • 500 V Megger/PI • AC impedance test • Winding resistance The test results were satisfactory. Electrical testing on the field should be done in accordance with GEK 103566. Body Wedge View Towards Turbine End Retaining Ring Balance 